{
  "description": "Stock that comes in while on-hand is below zero first covers the shortfall (D-124, posting rules §5.1, W2-09)",
  "notes": "Amounts in paisa, quantities in thousandths. The units that cover it, n = min(−on hand, qty), were already sold at the average (0 when none was known); correction = their real cost (value × n ÷ qty, half away from zero; the whole value when n = qty) − n × the average. A positive correction is Dr COGS / Cr INVENTORY. The average stays while on-hand stays below zero; at 0 or above it is the incoming cost, as before.",
